id: pm-web-apu6
title: Separate public legal templates from hosted deployment notices
description: "Audit publishable pm-web legal/privacy artifacts and replace hosted-service-specific identity, domains, retention, subprocessors, and data-flow claims with safe reusable package templates plus a private deployment overlay contract."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: legal-boundary,privacy,public-package,self-hosted
created_at: "2026-07-11T13:45:34.594Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-12T14:37:57.839Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-11T13:56:59.241Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Public package contains no hosted controller identity/domain or deployment-specific legal claims; default pages clearly require operator-supplied review; optional legal directory overlay is path-safe and documented; focused tests and package checks pass.
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Removed hosted-service-specific legal content from package artifacts, implemented a fail-closed private overlay boundary, documented operator/contributor responsibilities, and verified typecheck, 67 tests, production build, zero-vulnerability audit, 203-file dry-run package contents, sensitive-pattern scan, and diff integrity."
expected_result: Publishable pm-web artifacts remain operator-neutral and deployments can supply all reviewed legal pages privately without upstreaming hosted configuration or data.
actual_result: The package now serves explicit generic placeholders by default; PM_WEB_LEGAL_DIR provides an all-or-nothing path-safe private overlay; tests and package scans prevent hosted identifiers and claims from returning.
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T13:53:53.710Z",codex,"Audit finding: the publishable legal pages and README previously mixed reusable package artifacts with a named hosted operator/contact/address, hosted-service domains, jurisdiction/regulator references, retention/logging assertions, integration data-flow assertions, and hosted-service terms. No concrete credentials, tokens, private keys, production data, or production-derived fixtures were found in the npm publish set. Public GitHub repository metadata and generic example.com form placeholders are intentional package-source/example values."
  "2026-07-11T13:56:51.471Z",codex,"Residual governance consideration: the replaced hosted-service notices remain in existing Git history and may exist in previously published package versions. Current source and the next package artifact are clean, but history rewriting, registry deprecation/replacement, cache handling, or data-subject decisions require a separate deliberate release/governance action and were not performed in this no-commit/no-push task."
  "2026-07-12T14:37:57.830Z",codex,"Verification correction 2026-07-12: the inherited uncommitted item claimed anonymized public pages and overlay routing, but the working tree still contained hosted personal contact/address/domain terms and no overlay resolver. The source, tests, and generated artifacts now actually implement the stated boundary; 65 tests, build, audit, pack, and container checks pass."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T13:53:54.894Z",codex,"A reusable npm package cannot safely ship a hosted operator's legal promises. Keep bundled pages visibly non-legal placeholders and make the deployment overlay absolute, complete, path-contained, and startup-failing so production cannot silently mix package placeholders with private notices."
  "2026-07-11T13:53:56.459Z",codex,This host's npm user config defines allow-scripts in a form npm 11 injects into audit/pack and rejects for project-scoped operations. Isolating NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null validates public registry audit/pack without modifying or exposing the host credential-bearing npm config.
files[8]{path,scope,note}:
  package.json,project,Publish generic legal boundary guide with npm artifacts
  public/cookie-settings.html,project,Technical package storage inventory placeholder
  public/index.html,project,Generic package-default storage banner
  public/legal-common.css,project,Prominent template warning styling
  public/legal-notice.html,project,Generic package legal-notice placeholder
  public/privacy-policy.html,project,Generic package privacy placeholder
  public/terms.html,project,Generic package terms placeholder
  src/app.ts,project,Fail-closed operator legal overlay resolution and routing
